4. Core Components

4.1 Frontend (S3 Static Hosting)

Responsibilities:
	•	user interaction
	•	domain management UI
	•	query input
	•	display results

Must include:
	•	user authentication integration
	•	API integration

⸻

4.2 API Gateway

Responsibilities:
	•	request routing
	•	authentication integration
	•	throttling

Routes:
	•	/query → Query Lambda
	•	/domains → Domain Lambda

⸻

4.3 Domain Management Lambda

Responsibilities:
	•	create/update/delete domains
	•	store domain configuration
	•	trigger metadata generation

Data store:
	•	DynamoDB (Domain Registry)

⸻

4.4 Domain Registry (DynamoDB)

Stores domain configuration:

Example:

{
  "domain": "cloud_resources",
  "status": "active",
  "catalog_s3_path": "s3://dataset-catalog/cloud_resources/",
  "generator_config": {
    "include_tables": ["service_catalog"],
    "exclude_tables": ["tmp_*"]
  },
  "active_version": "v1"
}

4.5 Generator Trigger Lambda

Responsibilities:
	•	validate domain config
	•	enqueue generation task to SQS

⸻

4.6 SQS Queue

Responsibilities:
	•	decouple API from generator
	•	ensure reliability
	•	support retry

⸻

4.7 Metadata Generator Lambda

Responsibilities:
	•	scan database schema
	•	generate dataset definitions
	•	generate metadata:
	•	descriptions
	•	keywords
	•	example queries
	•	write dataset catalog to S3

Output:

S3://dataset-catalog/{domain}/{version}/

4.8 Dataset Catalog (S3)

Stores dataset metadata only (NO real data)

Example:

dataset: services
table: service_catalog

fields:
  - service_name
  - department


4.9 Query Orchestrator Lambda

Core runtime component.

Responsibilities:
	1.	receive user query
	2.	load domain config
	3.	load dataset catalog (from S3)
	4.	retrieve relevant datasets (optional)
	5.	call LLM planner
	6.	generate QuerySpec
	7.	validate QuerySpec
	8.	resolve dataset
	9.	build SQL
	10.	execute query
	11.	return result

⸻

4.10 Database (Aurora PostgreSQL)

Requirements:
	•	read-only access
	•	query timeout enforced
	•	limited result size

⸻

4.11 External LLM Service

Used for:
	•	QuerySpec generation

Input:
	•	user question
	•	dataset metadata

Must NOT include:
	•	real data
	•	sensitive information

⸻

